---
description: Prefer PowerShell for CLI/MR steps; use temp files for glab multiline
alwaysApply: true
globs: ["**/*"]
---

When running shell/CLI commands in this project:

1. Prefer PowerShell-native syntax (PowerShell here-strings, variables, and temp files) over bash heredocs.
2. For `glab` commands that take multiline text (for example `glab mr create --description`):
   - In PowerShell, write the multiline description/body to a temp file first (using `[System.IO.Path]::GetTempFileName()` and `Set-Content -NoNewline`).
   - Then pass the value to `glab` using `--description (Get-Content $tmp -Raw)` (or `--description-file` if supported by your `glab` version).
   - Delete the temp file afterwards.

